{
  "$comment": "Coverage map: source document -> implementation. See docs/COVERAGE.md for how to extend it.",
  "sourceDocument": {
    "title": "Invincible - Superhero Roleplaying (Free League / Skybound), core rulebook",
    "edition": "Core rules, first printing. No expansions.",
    "formSupplied": "Eight markdown chapter extracts (Ch.1&2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9) plus page images for a handful of tables, supplied in conversation during the build sessions.",
    "availableToThisRepo": false,
    "availabilityNote": "The extracts were never committed - they are the user's own book and are out of scope for this repository (section 11). Every entry below is therefore SEEDED from CLAUDE.md's extraction ledger and System Profile, which were written while the extracts were in hand. See caveats."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "WHAT THIS PROVES: that a named code artefact exists for each listed requirement. Nothing more.",
    "WHAT IT DOES NOT PROVE: that the implementation is CORRECT. A constant can exist and hold wrong values; a function can exist and compute the wrong thing. Where correctness matters, the marker points at a behavioural test in tests/run.js instead of at the implementation - see every A-* entry.",
    "PROVENANCE: entries marked provenance 'project-ledger' were seeded from CLAUDE.md, not read off the source document in this session. That buys REGRESSION detection (an implemented feature losing its implementation) but NOT OMISSION detection (a rule in the book that nobody ever noticed). Omission detection needs the extracts re-supplied and each entry promoted to provenance 'source'.",
    "A seeded entry must never be silently promoted to provenance 'source'. Promotion requires reading the cited chapter.",
    "COUNTS ARE NOT A SCORE: the denominator is the ledger's view of the book, not the book. A 100% figure here would mean 'everything we wrote down is implemented', which is a weaker claim than it looks."
  ],
  "statusMeanings": {
    "implemented": "A marker exists and the requirement is believed fully met.",
    "partial": "Implemented in part. The note says what is missing. Never a parking space for unchecked work.",
    "deliberately-omitted": "Out of scope by a recorded ruling. The note cites it.",
    "unknown": "Not checked, or the source material was never supplied. The note says which."
  },
